#### `lib.lists.sortOn`

Sort a list based on the default comparison of a derived property `b`.

The items are returned in `b`-increasing order.

**Performance**:

The passed function `f` is only evaluated once per item,
unlike an unprepared [`sort`](/manual/nixpkgs/unstable/#function-library-lib.lists.sort "lib.lists.sort") using `f p < f q`.

**Laws**:

    sortOn f == sort (p: q: f p < f q)

##### Inputs

`f`
1. Function argument

`list`
2. Function argument

##### Type

    sortOn :: (a -> b) -> [a] -> [a], for comparable b

##### Examples

**Example 186. `lib.lists.sortOn` usage example**

    sortOn stringLength [ "aa" "b" "cccc" ]
    => [ "b" "aa" "cccc" ]

